stack<int> st;  st.push(x); st.top(); st.pop(); st.empty(); st.size();
queue<int> q;   q.push(x);  q.front(); q.back(); q.pop(); q.empty();
deque<int> dq;  dq.push_back(x); dq.push_front(x); dq.pop_back(); dq.pop_front();
                dq.front(); dq.back(); dq[i];   // random access too
```
✍️ All of these are O(1).
✍️ `pop()` returns **nothing** (void). Read `top()`/`front()` first, then `pop()`.
✍️ Calling `top()`/`front()`/`pop()` on an empty container is undefined behaviour — always check `empty()` first.
